Enhancement: Add `--migrate` option to `backup` for zip and 7z archives

Until now, backing up the contents of a zip or 7z archive required
extracting it to disk first.

`backup --migrate <file>` now backs up the entries of a zip or 7z
archive in place, preserving the paths inside the archive. The option
can be specified multiple times, in which case the entries of all
given archives are merged into a single snapshot, with zip and 7z
archives freely combinable (each archive's format is detected by its
magic bytes). The archives are never extracted to disk: entry
contents are decompressed on the fly and streamed to the repository,
so memory usage stays bounded no matter how large the archives are.
`restore` reproduces the entries byte for byte, including
permissions and modification times. The archives are validated
before the repository is opened, and the backup always behaves like
`--force`, as the archives have no meaningful parent snapshot.

For 7z archives, the common compression methods are supported
(LZMA, LZMA2, Zstd, Deflate, Bzip2, LZ4, Brotli, PPMD, Delta, the
BCJ filters and stored data); encrypted or unsupported entries are
skipped with a warning.

